#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:66
msgid "Why does X need 5 secrets?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:68
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, the official X API splits auth across both app-level and "
"user-level credentials:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:70
msgid "`X_API_KEY` + `X_API_SECRET` identify your app"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:71
msgid "`X_BEARER_TOKEN` is used for app-level read access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:72
msgid ""
"`X_ACCESS_TOKEN` + `X_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET` let the CLI act as your user "
"account for writes and authenticated actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:74
msgid ""
"So yes — it is a lot of secrets for one integration, but this is the "
"stable official API path and is still preferable to cookie/session "
"scraping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:76
msgid "Setup requirements in the portal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:77
msgid "Create or open your app"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:78
msgid "In user authentication settings, set permissions to `Read and write`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:79
msgid ""
"Generate or regenerate the access token + access token secret after "
"enabling write permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:80
msgid ""
"Save all five values carefully — missing any one of them will usually "
"produce confusing auth or permission errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:82
msgid ""
"Note: upstream `x-cli` expects the full credential set to be present, so "
"even if you mostly care about read-only commands, it is simplest to "
"configure all five."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:84
msgid "Cost / Friction Reality Check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:86
msgid ""
"If this setup feels heavier than it should be, that is because it is. X’s"
" official developer flow is high-friction and often paid. This skill "
"chooses the official API path because it is more stable and maintainable "
"than browser-cookie/session approaches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xitter_SKILL.md:88
msgid ""
"If the user wants the least brittle long-term setup, use this skill. If "
"they want a zero-setup or unofficial path, that is a different trade-off "
"and not what this skill is for."
msgstr ""

